{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Find Rooms and Device Groups"},"description":"Find rooms/groups with IDs, etags, hierarchy, members, controllers, providers and messages. Query by name; follow pages; disambiguate by parentPath. Pages omit route declarations; id reads one group with them and payload shapes; merged IDs return redirectedFrom. Copy IDs/etags.\n\nUse control on the complete logical group; Port OS selects native/equivalent member delivery. Native capabilities/membershipComplete prove no aggregate coverage. membershipComplete=false means incomplete; absent means unknown. Empty resolved members do not prove an empty native group. Disabled routes cannot control; disabled groups need re-enablement through group_manage.\n\nControllers accept group-scoped actions: to clean a room, find the room group by name, read its controllers (endpointId and the messages each accepts, such as clean-room), then control that vacuum with {\"groupIds\":[\"<group ID>\"]}. To list a vacuum's rooms, query {\"controllers\": {\"has\": \"<vacuum endpoint ID>\"}}. Requested maps use endpoint_show on that controller, primary house-map; never draw geometry. expand selects observations; forceDeviceAttributeQuery refreshes them. Omitted/failed fresh values are unavailable. Disabled groups are hidden unless enablement=DISABLED or *.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"enablement":{"default":"ENABLED","description":"Filter by ENABLED (default), DISABLED, or * for both. This filter is preserved by pagination; id reads ignore it.","enum":["ENABLED","DISABLED","*"],"type":"string"},"expand":{"description":"Select declared capabilities whose route observations to return, for example [\"speaker\", \"media-player\"]. Requires id. This adds state readings to the selected group; it does not expand group membership or send commands. Expanding spatial returns raw room geometry for reading only. To show a map or let someone pick rooms, call endpoint_show on the vacuum with primary house-map; never draw one yourself.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"forceDeviceAttributeQuery":{"description":"Requires id and nonempty expand; refresh provider state before returning route observations.","type":"boolean"},"id":{"description":"Return one group by its returned group ID. Cannot be combined with query, maxResults or nextToken.","type":"string"},"maxResults":{"description":"Maximum number of groups (default 25, maximum 100).","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"nextToken":{"description":"Opaque cursor returned by a previous group_query call with the same query and maxResults.","type":"string"},"query":{"description":"Optional field-first filter. Omit it to load full context; filter only when the account is large. Each key is a field or a combinator, and all keys of one object must match: {\"role\": {\"eq\": \"ROOM\"}, \"name\": {\"like\": \"kitchen\"}}. Combinators: {\"and\": [query, ...]}, {\"or\": [query, ...]}, {\"not\": query}. Text operators: eq (exact), in (any of a list), like (case-insensitive substring), lt and gt (lexical order). List operators: has (contains the exact value), like (some value contains the substring, case-insensitive). Fields: id (text) returned group ID; name (text) group name; role (text) spatial role a provider declares: HOME, FLOOR, ROOM or ZONE; parentGroupId (text) ID of the containing group; ownerId (text, eq only at the top level) principal whose groups to list; defaults to the caller; children (list) IDs of contained groups; members (list) member endpoint IDs; controllers (list) IDs of endpoints that can act on the group, such as a robot that cleans the room; messages (list) returned message IDs the group itself accepts; providers (list) names of the plugins that report the group.","properties":{},"type":"object"}},"required":[],"type":"object"},"name":"group_query","outputSchema":{"$defs":{"ErrorCode":{"enum":["BAD_REQUEST","UN